  "source": {
    "title": "Dromore Leader, 7 September 1946, p. 3 (\"No Urban Council Election in Dromore\")",
    "publisher": "Dromore Leader (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "six nominated names plus two retiring members elected by the returning officer; eight of nine seats filled",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0005562/19460907/074/0003"
  },
  "note": "Whole-council election of the Dromore Urban Council under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946. Six nominations were received for the nine seats; the returning officer added two retiring members, making eight, and the ninth seat remained vacant (Dromore Leader, 7 September 1946, p. 3). Mr. Albert Cairns, town clerk and returning officer, elected Messrs. Hugh M'Fadden and Samuel J. Tinsley to bring the number to eight; the other seat remained vacant for the duration of the Council. Returned unopposed."
